issues.body:
This might be a subtle `tsconfig.json` settings issue.

Given: I have a TypeScript project that compiles without errors.
When: I import a function from Remeda into my TS project: `import { omit } from 'remeda';`

I Expect: the project will continue to compile without errors.
Instead I see: the project fails to compile with errors about `isPromise<T>()`:

```
> tsc --project ./tsconfig.build.json 
....
node_modules/remeda/dist/commonjs/guards.d.ts:67:56 - error TS2677: A type predicate's type must be assignable to its parameter's type.
  Type 'DefinitelyPromise<T>' is not assignable to type 'T'.
    'T' could be instantiated with an arbitrary type which could be unrelated to 'DefinitelyPromise<T>'.

67 export declare function isPromise<T>(data: T): data is DefinitelyPromise<T>;
```

Additional context:

I notice that `guards.isPromise<>()` has a lint override:

```TypeScript
// @ts-expect-error
export function isPromise<T>(data: T): data is DefinitelyPromise<T> {
  return data instanceof Promise;
}
```

The comment is preserved into `guards.js`:

```
// @ts-expect-error
export function isPromise(data) {
    return data instanceof Promise;
}
```

...but not into `guards.d.ts`

```TypeScript 
export declare function isPromise<T>(data: T): data is DefinitelyPromise<T>;
```
This shouldn't affect `tsc`, but may indicate that there was, at one time, tooling that complained about it. I'm wondering if it's sensitive to certain tsconfig.json settings?

